WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.857
Cleaning, parsing, validation, and verification are different tasks.

00:00:03.857 --> 00:00:06.412
Cleaning changes known formatting noise.

00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:12.247
Parsing extracts meaningful components. Validation checks whether a value follows a rule.

00:00:12.247 --> 00:00:16.187
Verification asks whether the value corresponds to reality.

00:00:16.187 --> 00:00:21.587
Keeping these tasks separate makes a preparation pipeline easier to reason about and audit.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:25.522
Text cleaning should separate normalization from interpretation.

00:00:25.522 --> 00:00:30.457
Trimming spaces or standardizing case is usually safe when the rule is documented;

00:00:30.457 --> 00:00:35.622
correcting a person's name or guessing an email address is a much stronger intervention.

00:00:35.622 --> 00:00:38.720
Preserve the original value when auditability matters.
